{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">Markdown converters typically pass raw HTML through unchanged, so a model reply piped into dangerouslySetInnerHTML can execute a script or an onerror handler exactly like a malicious form field would.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Run the converted HTML through a sanitizer like DOMPurify before it reaches the DOM, strip scripts, event handler attributes, and javascript: URLs while keeping real formatting intact.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Treat model output as untrusted input regardless of provider or prompt design, sanitize as a second independent layer alongside a strict CSP, and keep the sanitizer library itself updated as new bypass techniques get discovered.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
